[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Bounded analog XSPICE summer preparation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEM-XSPICE-SUMMER-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Prepare exact bounded voltage-vector summer relations
STATEMENT: >>>
The frontend shall prepare analog summer models with 2..16 noninverted scalar voltage inputs in a generated vector port and one scalar voltage output. Each input may retain differential polarity. The output relation shall be out_gain*sum(in_gain[i]*(input[i]+in_offset[i]))+out_offset, with per-input defaults in_gain=1 and in_offset=0 and output defaults out_gain=1 and out_offset=0. Explicit arrays shall match input count, use generated scalar-value recognition and existing lexical parameter evaluation, and retain physical source locations. Unsupported types, lengths, duplicate or unknown parameters, nonfinite expressions and opaque syntax shall produce no partial relation.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: XspiceSyntax.cs, ScalarVectorExtraction.cs, DeclarationExtraction.cs, XspiceSummerLowering.cs. Verification: XspiceSummerTests includes malformed arrays, ports, lengths, finite arithmetic and a reproducible FsCheck campaign; XspiceSummerOracleIntegration compares original A/model cards in DC, complex AC and transient with analytical references and existing typed elements on both providers. Corpus inspection is lexical and does not establish full-deck execution. Parent worktree owns bridge integration. Evidence: evidence/xspice-summer.json and docs/xspice-summer-results.md. Requirement remains Draft.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEM-XSPICE-SUMMER-EXEC-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Execute the original voltage summer through the public bridge
STATEMENT: >>>
Selected preparation shall emit the complete admitted differential summer relation through existing controlled-voltage elements, keeping auxiliary nodes out of original root observations. Constant synthetic bias shall have explicit zero AC excitation. Only the original output branch shall carry native branch identity. Expansion budgets and atomic refusal shall remain enforced.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: OperatingPointBridge summer dispatch and CircuitReadiness structural admission. Verification: PreparationSemanticsTests and XspiceSummerOracleIntegration now use actual generated selection and the typed client for original default, weighted and differential A/model cards in DC, complex AC and ramp transient on LU/faer. Initial helper-only qualification remains historical evidence. The integrated focused run includes 36 tests and 78 native output comparisons; unrelated models in the measured summer roots remain blockers.
<<<
